Steve,ascended

Yay, my first ascension! It only took me seven years!

There weren't any real surprises. Got my blessed +3 gdsm from quaffing
a  fountain, and the rest flowed from that. Went down to Minetown--no
magic  lamps--bummed around for a bit, then went to the bottom and
picked up the  booze and the luckstone. I double-dipped the booze on
the Oracle level to  get some water, then made some holy water to
bless the luckstone. Huge  hardware store on level 5, but no magic
lamps or magic markers. There were a  couple bags of tricks, though,
which were useful. After the mines, I went to  Sokoban and picked up
my amulet of reflection.

Not many altars this game: the one in minetown was not co-aligned, and
I  didn't feel like killing a priest in case he was the only one from
whom I  could buy protection. There was one by itself on level 4, and
a lawful altar  with attendant priest on level 14. On level 17, I was
robbing a magic memory  vault and triggered a magic portal. Awesome!
One bloodbath later (Croesus  does some major damage with that sword
of his), I was a very rich man, and  bought all my protection. A
little polypiling got me a +2 T-shirt and a +1  oilskin cloak, both
blessed. Glee!

Quest was a little harder than I expected; last time I attempted it, I
had  the teleport and teleport control intrinsics, so once Thoth Amon
started  whaling on me I simply teleported to the upstairs, and
smacked him down at  my leisure. This time, it was a little rougher,
and one time I had a brief  scare when he attacked me at the same time
an Elvenking showed up; I was  pretty sure that the Wizard was the
only one who could duplicate, but I was  willing to believe anything
of Thoth Amon. But, in the end, I did take him  down, and the Heart of
Ahriman was mine.

Medusa was a piece of cake: took one look at me and turned to stone; I
was  surprised, inasmuch as I don't remember her doing that, and I've
had  reflection before when facing her. Maybe it was the looking glass
I was  carrying. Whatever; no boots of levitation/shield of reflection
in the  Perseus statue, but I had a ring of levitation and the Heart,
and my little  amulet of reflection, so no worries.

On to the castle; it went down a lot like Fort Ludios: hang around the
 doorway and take them out one at a time. By this time I had Cleaver
from  #offering, so things were going down pretty quick. Got the wand;
a scroll of  identify I was carrying told me that it had two charges.
Wished for 2  blessed scrolls of charging; got one. Used my second
wish for some blessed  fireproof +2 speed boots. I already had some
gauntlets of dexterity that I  picked up somewhere, so I recharged the
wand and started wishing for magic  markers. I wrote a couple blessed
scrolls of genocide and got rid of L's and  c's (I've had two
promising characters die because they were wielding  cockatrice
corpses and fell into trap doors, so now they are a  must-genocide),
and then it was enchant armor all the way (I did write a few  enchant
weapon, mostly to get Cleaver up to +7). I got my gdsm up to +5, but 
everything else stopped at +4; my AC was -38 at this point, so I
decided to  let things be.

I'd been through Hell a few times before (got one barbarian up to the
astral  plane, but didn't know how to discriminate one altar from
another, so I  sacrificed the amulet to Set; Crom was most
displeased), so I knew pretty  much what to expect, and there wasn't
anything really scary. I bribed  Baalzebub and Asmodeus, and slew
Orcus pretty handily; he even had a charge  left on his wand when he
"gave" it to me.

The Wizard was kind to me this time around; he only appeared 5 times,
and he  did not deign to dodge the death rays I zapped at him. His
loss, I suppose.  A few scary moments in Moloch's sanctum, but I got
the Amulet and began  high-tailing it for the entrance. I got waylaid
around level 15, I think, by  a titan who began summoning all sorts of
nasty creatures. I wanted to just  bypass him, but I had to take him
out. Running, running, running up the  stairs, and finally I make it
to the Planes.

Earth was easy; I had 7 wands of digging. Air had some scary moments,
but I  made it through, thanks to some kindly energy vortices that
sheltered me  while I caught my breath from the air elementals. Fire
was arduous; it took  me forever to find the portal. Water was a
breeze.

Astral plane...oh, the astral plane. I was lucky this time around;
never ran  into Famine. I killed pestilence 3 times and Death 5, but
no Famine. Just as  well. First altar I went to was attended by Set's
high priest, but the  second one was right on the money; high priest
of Crom gave me two bits for  an ale, and next turn I began my life as
a demigod.

